WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
[Upbeat intro music]

2
00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.326
Hello!. Welcome to Web Demystified.

3
00:00:03.326 --> 00:00:08.031
I’m Jeremie and in this series of videos we are gonna try to make the web easy.

4
00:00:08.031 --> 00:00:13.358
So today, in this special episode, I’m gonna give you a quick overview of what the web is and how it works.

5
00:00:13.358 --> 00:00:14.908
Lame!

6
00:00:15.698 --> 00:00:21.157
Yeah! Maybe there will be stuff you already know, but you could be surprised.

7
00:00:21.157 --> 00:00:24.417
And if you’re not, show this video to someone who will be!

8
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:26.920
Anyway, we have to start somewhere… so let’s go!

9
00:00:32.348 --> 00:00:35.667
Everything starts with your favorite browser where you type a web address.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.640
Nope! I use Google.

11
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:46.300
Yes… and Google, like any other search engine that you could use, is nothing but a web site for which you have to type its web address.

12
00:00:46.303 --> 00:00:53.276
Ok don’t worry, this is just an overview. We will talk about search engines and searching the web in another video.

13
00:00:53.276 --> 00:00:55.101
So as you type a web address…

14
00:00:55.101 --> 00:01:01.619
The technical name for a web address is a URL (Uniform Resource Locator)…

15
00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:06.777
and it’s maybe better to save that for another video.

16
00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:09.146
Overview… remember, overview.

17
00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:12.190
So as you type a web address and hit the “Enter” key

18
00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.887
OR click a link from a search page

19
00:01:13.887 --> 00:01:19.816
your browser will send a request to the server that hosts the web site that lives at that address.

20
00:01:19.816 --> 00:01:24.285
There, the server will process the address and it will send you back an HTML document.

21
00:01:25.142 --> 00:01:33.804
And, yes, we will get into the details of how server and request work… in another video.

22
00:01:33.804 --> 00:01:37.920
Next, the browser retrieves the HTML document and it reads it.

23
00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:45.694
Usually, the HTML document contains further information telling the web browser that it needs some extra resources to render the full page.

24
00:01:45.694 --> 00:01:48.971
For example: stylesheets (to know how to display the document)

25
00:01:48.971 --> 00:01:49.971
images

26
00:01:49.971 --> 00:01:52.751
or even scripts (to attach special effects).

27
00:01:52.751 --> 00:01:58.767
Yes, you got it right… other videos to cover all of that.

28
00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.714
Your browser will request all those extra ressources

29
00:02:02.714 --> 00:02:09.704
and, once it gets all the resources, it will mix them all together to, at last, display the web page you were expecting.

30
00:02:10.023 --> 00:02:11.536
Okay, let's recap!

31
00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:16.963
The web is a collection of documents that will be requested by a browser from a server.

32
00:02:16.963 --> 00:02:20.697
Each document is accessible through a web address.

33
00:02:20.697 --> 00:02:27.250
The browser will mix all the necessary documents to turn any HTML document into a nice web page.

34
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.943
Yes, the web is nothing else than that.

35
00:02:29.943 --> 00:02:34.749
Of course that simplicity hides many subtle things. Things that we will explore…

36
00:02:34.749 --> 00:02:36.185
In another video!

37
00:02:37.059 --> 00:02:39.319
Well… maybe more than one.

38
00:02:40.142 --> 00:02:42.437
Thank you for watching our very first video.

39
00:02:42.437 --> 00:02:46.460
As you might guess, many others are in the pipe and they should arrive very soon.

40
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.937
If you liked it, share it with your friends.

41
00:02:48.937 --> 00:02:53.978
If you didn’t… I don't know, share it with your… arch enemy for example?

42
00:02:53.978 --> 00:02:59.725
If you want to continue the discussion feel free to comment down below or join me and my colleagues on Twitter.

43
00:02:59.725 --> 00:03:03.455
And until next time… Long live the open web! Bye!

44
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:23.000
[Upbeat outro music fadeout]
